there are no images of what's happening  inside managua's chipotle prison it's  where more than 40 government opponents  are being tried behind closed doors for  alleged conspiracy terrorism and much  more  human rights center director vilma nunes  calls it a judicial farce  they've not been able to prove any crime  against these people who have been  practically kidnapped and kept in prison  violating the law and denying them due  process there's no presumption of  innocence the lawyers have had no access  to them until the day of the trial  this is a model of an isolation cell  where nuna says the accused suffer from  cruel and inhumane treatment including  torture  would be presidential candidate felix  maradiada faces up to 24 years in prison  for leading an opposition coalition that  demanded free and transparent elections  last year  his wife who says she and their daughter  were forced to flee nicaragua believes a  guilty verdict is a foregone conclusion  i think the hardest part is having to  console our eight-year-old daughter  knowing that he might be arrested felix  sent her a taped message saying he loved  her and would always be thinking of her  but it's difficult  president ortega began arresting his  staunchest opponents including seven  presumptive presidential candidates six  months before november's elections  he ran and won a fourth consecutive term  virtually unopposed but the elections  were widely dismissed as a sham  four members of carlos fernando  chamorro's family are now being tried  we are facing a great injustice based on  political vengeance not just my sister  christiana but my brother pedro joaquin  and two cousins all of the prisoners are  innocent and are being tried for  participating in civic protests because  they represent the desire of nicaraguans  to hold free elections  former ortega ally dora maria deyes an  emblematic rebel commander during the  1970s sandinista revolution is also  being tried this week on charges of  treason  as is 24 year old lester aleman a  student leader who helped organize mass  protests against ortega in 2018.  ortega has ignored widespread  international appeals to release the  opposition prisoners preferring it seems  to make an example of those whom he  accuses of trying to overthrow his  government  but by tightening control and  encouraging more nicaraguans to join the  tens of thousands who've already fled  the country the trials could end up  making the country's political crisis  even worse  lucia newman al jazeera
 

